SUMMARY:Night Shift at Lancaster Science Factory
DESCRIPTION:Overview\nExperience the Lancaster Science Factory in a whole new way when you stay overnight! Explore over 75 hands-on exhibits\, enjoy a pre-lights-out snack\, unroll your sleeping bag in the exhibit hall\, and have a light breakfast before you leave in the morning. New to this year\, educators will be leading hands-on STEM workshops in our Maker Space! Consider joining us for the Night Shift with your scout group\, sports team or even for a special birthday!  \nDates\n\n\n\nSaturday\, November 7 – Sunday\, November 8\, 2026\n\nClick here to register \n\n\nSaturday\, December 5 – Sunday\, December 6\, 2026 \n\nClick here to register\n\n\nSaturday\, February 13 – Sunday\, February 14\, 2027 \n\nClick here to register\n\n\nSaturday\, April 17 – Sunday\, April 18\, 2027 \nClick here to register \n\n\n\nItinerary \n\n\n\n6:30-7:00 pm: Arrival\, check-in \n7:00-10:00 pm: Museum exploration\, Science Cafe activity\, scavenger hunts\, workshops \n7:15-7:55: Group A workshop \n8:05-8:45: Group B workshop \n8:55-9:25: Group C workshop \n10:00-10:30 pm: Set up sleeping accommodations \n10:30 pm: Get ready for lights out \n7:00-8:00 am: Light breakfast available \n8:30 am: Exhibit hall closes \n\n\n\nQuestions? Reach out to mstoltzfus@tlsf.org
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/night-shift-at-lancaster-science-factory/2026-11-07/
LOCATION:Lancaster Science Factory\, 454 New Holland Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Autumn,Children & Family Events,Classes,Community Interest,Lancaster City,Spring,Winter
